f you  actually look at the month by month  numbers there's no change in the number  of families in May relative to April  that are approaching the border so it's  not even working as a deterrent which I  think over the long term may be a reason  that he decides to turn away from it  Philip let's turn to Paul Manafort he  spent his first night in jail why did  the judge jail Paul Manafort well  essentially judge jailed Paul Manafort  because she had lost confidence that he  would essentially behave properly well  he was out on bail that he was accused  by special counsel robert muller of a  witness tampering of reaching out to  someone who could testify against him to  try and get their story straight  essentially and so the judge sent him to  jail because she didn't try  said he would she said you know I can't  just take your phone away this isn't  middle school how extreme is this I mean  it's not I wouldn't say it's terribly  extreme if you violate the terms of your  bail then sometimes you have to go to  jail so this is not as president Trump  said because they think he's a big  dangerous mob boss it's cuz he simply  didn't adhere to the rules that he was  supposed to follow at the same time I  mean Paul Manafort is someone who is  accustomed to a certain lifestyle or  wearing $7,000 suit he has an apartment  in Trump Tower so could there perhaps be  pressure on man afford now enhanced  pressure in a way that there wasn't  before that might in fact lead to him  cooperating with the special counsel  well I think that yes I think that  special counsel Muller's not terribly  upset that Paul Manafort has to go to  jail  obviously the special counsel is trying  to put a lot of pressure on mana for  wants him to tell him whatever he  happens to know about President Trump  about the Trump campaign this is  certainly going to be an incentive for  Paul man afford to try and figure out  okay I need to change something I can't  be here very long maybe making a deal is  the way to do it at the same time  according to a CBS news report Michael  Cohen believes that President Trump and  his allies may be turning on him what do  we know about that situation and how  great a threat is going do we think at  this point I mean honestly I think Cohen  is one of the biggest threats to  President Trump and the reason why is  because folks should remember Cohen  started working for the Trump  Organization back in 2007 so he was  there for nine years essentially before  the Trump air campaign got started he  knows all of the deals that Trump was  making he was Trump's so-called fixer he  was a guy sent out to deal with little  messes he knows a lot of stuff he was  there during the campaign he's mentioned  in the infamous steel dossier he  obviously set up the deal with stormy  Daniels the adult film actress there are  all sorts of lots of information that  Michael Cohen has so I'm not surprised  that Donald Trump's getting a little  nervous about it all right Phillip bump  thanks so much for being with us happy  Father's Day Phillip thank you sir
 

